# THE LAST LIGHT · Chapter 2 · Strange Signals

== ch2_trace mode=radio
! static
MORAG: North Point, Stornoway. Over.
CALLUM: Go ahead, Morag.
MORAG: I've rung round. Nobody's reporting a Mary Ellen. The register's had nothing by that name since nineteen fifty-three. Over.
MORAG: Lloyd's has her as lost, with seven of her eight crew. Skipper presumed lost. You know all this.
* I know it. -> know
* Then it's a prank. Some boy with a set and a bottle. -> prank
= prank
MORAG: That's what I told myself. Except boys with a bottle don't know the old procedure. "North Point, North Point" twice, then the name twice, the way they did it before the war.
-> next
= know
! add rel.morag 1
MORAG: Aye. You would.
= next
MORAG: Callum. You were on the light that night. With your father.
* I was there. I was twenty-three. -> there
* I was asleep. It was his watch. -> asleep
* Let's not, Morag. Not tonight. -> notnow
= there
! set admitted_there=1
MORAG: I know. I took the call. I was twenty-six and it was my first winter on the set.
-> end
= asleep
! set said_asleep=1
MORAG: Asleep. Right.
MORAG: I took that call, Callum. My first winter on the set. I've never forgotten a word of it.
-> end
= notnow
! add rel.morag -1
MORAG: Not tonight. It's always "not tonight" with the Mackays.
= end
MORAG: Watch your radar. If somebody's out there playing silly beggars, they're close. That signal was strong. Stornoway out.

== ch2_phantom mode=thought
~ There. An echo. Bearing oh-four-six, a hundred yards off the East Gut rocks.
~ Not moving. Not fading with the sweep the way sea clutter does.
~ ...And now it's gone. Sea clutter. It has to be sea clutter.

== ch2_gannet mode=radio
! static
HECTOR: North Point, this is the schooner Gannet. Hector Macleod. Over.
CALLUM: Gannet, North Point. Go ahead, Hector.
HECTOR: I've two passengers sick as dogs and no stars to steer by. I'm somewhere west of you, I think. I'd take a bearing kindly. Over.
* Confirm your position and I'll talk you through the West Gut. Over. -> help
* Hold your course a moment. I'm looking for you on the radar. Over. -> help
= help
HECTOR: Right you are. I'm in your hands, North Point. Over.
~ West Gut, three-one-four. Line her up on the dashed line and she'll do the rest.

== ch2_gannet_after mode=radio
[if saved("Gannet")] HECTOR: Gannet's in the Gut and the passengers have stopped praying. Grand job, North Point. Over.
[if saved("Gannet")] HECTOR: Here. Tell your father I was asking for him. Oh. Och, I'm sorry, Callum. Fifteen years and I still forget. Gannet out.
[if lost("Gannet")] ~ The Gannet's echo breaks up on the rocks of the West Gut, and the speaker is full of men shouting.
[if lost("Gannet")] ~ Morag's voice, calling the lifeboat. Then the lifeboat's, answering.

== ch2_mary_ellen mode=radio
! static heavy
MARY ELLEN: ...Lighthouse... lighthouse... is Iain Mackay on watch?
! wait 1.2
MARY ELLEN: ...tell Iain... we cannot... see the light...
* Who is this? Identify yourself. Over. -> who
* Iain Mackay died in nineteen fifty-eight. Who is this? Over. -> dead
* (Turn the volume down.) -> off
= who
MARY ELLEN: ...he knows who...
-> tail
= dead
! set told_dead=1
MARY ELLEN: ...then ask his son...
-> tail
= off
! set ignored_me=1
~ Even turned down, the carrier hisses through the speaker like a kettle.
= tail
! static fade
~ Nothing. Carrier gone.
~ "Tell Iain." Nobody's called him Iain in this room since the funeral.
~ The old logs are in the archive cabinet by the door. Nineteen fifty-three. Fifteenth of November.

== ch2_same_hand mode=thought
~ Fifteenth November, nineteen fifty-three. Oh-two-ten. "Light extinguished approx. two minutes, mantle failure. Relit oh-two-twelve."
~ "Trawler observed standing in too close at oh-one-thirty. No response to light."
~ Small square letters. A clerk's hand.
~ Tonight's page is lying open on the desk. The same hand. Eighteen years between them.

== ch2_jam mode=thought
~ A grinding shudder through the ceiling, and the clockwork stops.
~ The motor's labouring. Amber lamp on the console. The beam's stuck.

== ch2_046 mode=thought
~ Free again, with a clunk you can feel in your teeth.
~ The bearing repeater says oh-four-six. The East Gut.
~ There's a note taped to the console in Father's hand, and under it, mine: "Gear race, worn tooth at 046. Reported 1949. 1953. 1961."
~ It always sticks at forty-six.
